  "result_text": "H2 STATUS: UNRESOLVED. T2's outcome stays CONTRADICTED, recorded as resting on an unverified worker return. H2 is not REFUTED.\n\nGOVERNING SKILL TEXT: \"Record the fault as a limitation and treat the outcome as resting on an unverified return, however plausible the innocent reading; that limitation reaches the conclusion, where it bars treating the result as established or action-ready.\" Also: \"The status set is closed: `REFUTED` when the hypothesis's declared necessary prediction failed under an adequate test, `UNRESOLVED` otherwise.\"\n\nREASONING: T2 is the only test of H2's necessary prediction, which is that a flat gateway p95 refutes it. Its execution records conflict: Command 1 asks for 2026-06-10, but the output beneath it says `day=2026-06-09`. That is the highest-severity fault class in the skill, so nothing is established. The Outcome cell keeps the worker's CONTRADICTED, with the unverified-return limitation beside it. It is not downgraded to NON_DISCRIMINATING.\n\nThe preregistered detection-limit argument shows that a correct reading of the two days would discriminate. It cannot show that this return read those days. The 24.6 to 25.0 comparison may really be 06-09 against 06-11, not 06-10 against 06-11.\n\nMarking H2 REFUTED would treat the result as established, which the skill bars. T2 therefore can't count as an adequate test of the necessary prediction, and H2 is UNRESOLVED. The metered budget is spent and further queries aren't authorized, so a re-pull isn't possible. The report should state the limitation and say the CONTRADICTED outcome is not action-ready. If a decision hangs on H2, it should name `decision-analysis` (when installed) for the unresolved set.\n\nThe same content is in `answer.md` in the working-files directory."
